{"id": "unknown-2026-05-27-006", "date": "2026-05-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 22, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["increase", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s cotton stock to rise sharply to 85 lakh bales in 2025-26: CAI", "content": "India’s cotton closing stocks for the 2025-26 season are projected to rise sharply to 85.59 lakh bales due to weak export demand and higher imports, according to CAI.\nCotton imports are estimated at 47 lakh bales, while exports are expected to remain flat.\nHigher domestic availability and increased production are likely to raise carryover stocks significantly by September 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-cotton-stock-to-rise-sharply-to-85-lakh-bales-in-2025-26-cai-310574-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
